@startuml software-architecture
' Created by GPT-6.1-Sol on behalf of Nico running in codex.
title Digital stethoscope — agreed software layer architecture
top to bottom direction
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false

rectangle "L2 — Application (L2_application/)" as L2 #E8F1FC {
  component "Controller\nMode state machine\nSingle writer of mode state" as Controller
  component "UI\nDisplay + operator interaction" as UI
  component "Shell\nConfiguration + evaluation commands" as Shell
}

rectangle "L1 — Services (L1_services/)" as L1 #E8F5E9 {
  component "Audio\nAcquisition, listening, capture, replay" as Audio
  component "BPM\nIndependent analysis path + quality gate" as BPM
  component "Storage\nSD access" as Storage
  component "Network / FHIR\nMeasurement export" as Network
  rectangle "dsp_core/ — pure C, no Zephyr headers" as DSP {
    component "Listening + analysis filters\nEnvelope / autocorrelation\nWSOLA replay" as Algorithms
  }
}

rectangle "L0 — Platform (L0_platform/)" as L0 #FFF3E0 {
  component "Thin driver + devicetree adapters\nI2S / GPIO / ADC / PWM / display / touch" as Adapters
}

rectangle "Zephyr — SOUP / operating system" as OS #EEEEEE {
  component "Drivers, DMA, interrupts\nKernel, queues, scheduling\nFilesystem + networking / TLS" as Zephyr
}

rectangle "MON/ — cross-cutting monitoring" as MON #FCE4EC {
  component "Read-only supervision\nWatchdog, stack / heap watermarks\nAudio deadlines + buffer errors\nBPM quality + test-source export guard" as Monitor
}

rectangle "common/ — shared contracts" as Common #F3E5F5 {
  component "AudioBlock\nControlEvent\nMeasurementResult" as Contracts
}

rectangle "tests/host/ — outside device runtime" as Tests {
  component "Host tests + recorded WAV evaluation" as HostTests
}

L2 -down-> L1 : service calls
L1 -down-> L0 : platform calls
L0 -down-> OS : Zephyr APIs
Audio -[norank]-> DSP : processing / replay
BPM -[norank]-> DSP : analysis
L1 -[hidden]right-> MON
L0 -[hidden]right-> Common
OS -[hidden]right-> Tests

legend bottom
  This is the agreed design documented in PR #15, not the current source layout.
  Calls go downward; upward communication uses message queues.
  L2 may also access L0 directly. L2, L1 and L0 may use common.
  common has no dependencies; MON observes all layers read-only.
  Zephyr owns HAL, DMA and interrupts; there is no project-owned HAL.
  Start on one core; extend only when measurements justify it.
endlegend
footer Created by GPT-6.1-Sol on behalf of Nico running in codex.
@enduml
